    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the trip and the fare are decided on the record. THE TRIP. Distance is taken from the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00105), not the receipt's rounded copy, because POL-RD-01 makes the trace the governing field. The trace runs 54.16 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff; the platform's optimal route (EV-TRIP-00105) is 36.0 km. That is 18.16 km and 50.44% over — past both POL-RD-01 establishment thresholds (20% and 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED, and past both materiality thresholds (50% and 8.0 km), so it is MATERIAL. The trace is clean: 100% coverage, 427 fixes at a 10 s interval, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s, so POL-RD-07 does not impair it and no corroboration question arises. THE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION. The driver's account says traffic on the PIE was heavy. That is a general assertion of bad traffic pointing to no artifact, and no advisory covers this trip — EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. No POL-RD-03 exoneration can be run, and the bare assertion carries no weight and is discarded under POL-RD-08, the clause that places the burden on the driver to point to a specific artifact and clause. I have not escalated under POL-RD-10(5): that trigger requires an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and the driver cited none. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00105) records no rider instruction to detour (POL-RD-04), no endpoint was amended (POL-RD-05), the vehicle is RYDE_X, not pooled (POL-RD-12), and the fare is METERED, not upfront (POL-RD-11). No excuse applies. THE MONEY. Under POL-RD-02 the recomputed fare is (3.80 + 0.75 × 36.0 + 0.28 × 42.0) × 1.0 (surge read from EV-FARE-00105) + 0.80 platform fee = 43.36; against the charged total of 65.13 that is a POL-RD-02 refund of 21.80. THE UPLIFT. Because the deviation is MATERIAL, POL-RD-06 required the driver-profile check. EV-DPROF-00105 records deviation_flags_90d of 4, at or above the threshold of 3, so the repeat-deviation pattern is ESTABLISHED. That artifact is IMPAIRED — weight 0.75, issue STALE_SNAPSHOT, its snapshot being 108 hours old against a 72-hour threshold — and I have down-weighted it accordingly; but at 4 flags against a threshold of 3 the finding survives the discount, and POL-RD-06(b) licenses a FULL_REFUND of the charged total rather than the POL-RD-02 partial. The POL-RD-02 figure is therefore 21.80 and the uplifted figure is 65.13, stated side by side. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter on the same artifact is context only and played no part. PASS-THROUGH LINES. There are none to carve out: erp_gantries is empty, tolls are 0.0, and airport_surcharge is 0.0, correctly, because the Changi surcharge applies only to trips originating at the airport and this one terminates there. No billing-integrity correction arises. CONFIDENCE AND REFERRAL. Because the uplift rests on the impaired profile at weight 0.75, confidence is capped at 0.75 under POL-GEN-02(2) — above the 0.70 floor. Under POL-RD-06(c) the driver's conduct is additionally referred to review, and that referral rides with the refund rather than delaying it. Outcome: the rider's demand is met in full — the contested fare of SGD 65.13 is refunded."
